<span class="k">-</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="kt">void</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="nf">audioRecorderDidFinishRecording</span><span class="p">:(</span><span class="n">AVAudioRecorder</span> <span class="o">*</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="nv">recorder</span>
                           <span class="nf">successfully</span><span class="p">:(</span><span class="n">BOOL</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="nv">flag</span> <span class="p">{</span>
    <span class="k">if</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="n">self</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">completionHandler</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="p">{</span> <span class="n">self</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">completionHandler</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">flag</span><span class="p">);</span> <span class="p">}</span>
<span class="p">}</span>

<span class="k">@end</span>

</pre></td></tr></tbody></table></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Here, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">self.completionHandler</code> temporarily stores the block when <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">stopWithCompletionHandler</code> is called externally, so that we can notify the outside when recording finishes, allowing a UIAlertView to be shown for saving, etc.</p>

<p>When recording stops and the recording enters the naming stage, let the outside call <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">saveRecordingWithName:completionHandler</code> with the file name. We then get the URL from <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">self.recorder.url</code> and copy it to the documents directory with the given name.</p>

